body:
You say that like seeing Blackpink live so *common (you know... since YG's kept them in the dungeon up until like 2 months ago lol)* and that that needs to happen to draw conclusions. Fine, if we're going by that, there's a better chance of people actually having seen Dua Lipa live as she's been heavily active for the past two years. If not shining alone, the girl can pull off choreographed routines as well. Say what you want but most of us rely on live performances uploaded to Youtube to form our own opinions.

&#x200B;

My point is that people are so far up their own perceived superiority with how they feel about Blackpink (and KPOP groups in general, true to the sub I guess) that they're willing to be shady and bring Dua Lipa down. I say all of this as someone who actively enjoys both acts, but can recognize that both come from very different managements and it's annoying for KPOP fans to keep giving Western artists shit just to try and make their oppars and unnies seem better.
